import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 398 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Inevitable Historical Regression: When a Major Power Falls, Civilization Breaks Generations","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 398 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Inevitable Historical Regression: When a Major Power Falls, Civilization Breaks Generations","no":398,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Ji Ning","Historical Regression","Major-Power Fall","Lineage Break"],"related":["07-Self-Generation Self-Growth Evolution Law","25-Symbiotic Feedback Loop Mechanism","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0398_模块2-莽荒纪-历史倒退必然性-大能陨落文明即断代.md","filePath":"en/0398_模块2-莽荒纪-历史倒退必然性-大能陨落文明即断代.md"}'),o={name:"en/0398_模块2-莽荒纪-历史倒退必然性-大能陨落文明即断代.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,c,g){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-398-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-inevitable-historical-regression-when-a-major-power-falls-civilization-breaks-generations" tabindex="-1">Entry 398 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Inevitable Historical Regression: When a Major Power Falls, Civilization Breaks Generations <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-398-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-inevitable-historical-regression-when-a-major-power-falls-civilization-breaks-generations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 398 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Inevitable Historical Regression: When a Major Power Falls, Civilization Breaks Generations&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 07, 25, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-every-great-calamity-is-a-civilization-zeroing" tabindex="-1">Introduction: every great calamity is a civilization zeroing <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-every-great-calamity-is-a-civilization-zeroing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: every great calamity is a civilization zeroing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the causal self-discipline axiom requires thoroughly rooting out civilizational regression and historical reversing; the collective ascension axiom requires strong ones to feed back to Myriad Ranks. This entry specializes in the Manghuang world&#39;s coldest structural law — <strong>the day a major power falls is the hour civilization breaks generations.</strong> The law-first axiom here is not rhetoric: Manghuang&#39;s regression is no accident, but the inevitable output of its &quot;lineage follows the person, resources perish with war&quot; law. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = high-leaning-medium. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>On the surface regression, but first point out the energy spinning behind it: Manghuang&#39;s strong ones pour massive energy into &quot;mutual-destruction-style&quot; great calamities — Three Realms war, Wujian Gate war; strong ones clashing&#39;s aftershocks flatten realm domains, evaporate spirit veins. This energy could have stabilized laws and reinforced worlds, yet in battle after battle between camps it turns to radioactive dust. <strong>The energy waste of major-power war is the first driving force of civilizational regression.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Manghuang&#39;s regression is the overlay of three iron laws:</p><ol><li><strong>Fall = break generations</strong>: once the Three Purities, Bodhi, Northern-Road Immortal level fall in battle, their lifetime comprehension of laws is buried with them; later cultivators grope the same road from scratch</li><li><strong>War = zeroing</strong>: after a great calamity, cave-heavens shatter, spirit veins sever, mortals die by the hundred million; civilization stock accumulated over ten million years physically returns to zero</li><li><strong>Raise = abandon</strong>: realm targets raised all the way; old realm domains, old arts are seen by new generations as &quot;low-tier,&quot; unmaintained, layer by layer abandoned — Three Realms in Chaos Immortal Realm&#39;s eyes are no more than a newbie village</li></ol><p>Conclusion: Manghuang&#39;s civilization curve is not rising, but &quot;spiral zeroing&quot; — every tier ascended, the tier underfoot rots.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Behind regression is the lone-path logic Ji Ning represents&#39;s disregard for &quot;civilization stock&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Values affection not institutions</strong>: Ji Ning bleeds for Yu Wei, for his tribe, yet never thinks &quot;how to make the next great war not zero things&quot;</li><li><strong>Strong ones as chess pieces</strong>: major powers in narrative are &quot;combat-power units&quot;; their Dao insights are not civilizational assets, but experience packs or cannon fodder on the protagonist&#39;s road</li><li><strong>Ascend = abandon</strong>: after cultivating to higher realms, duty to maintain lower realm domains is near zero — gone and no longer cares</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Manghuang&#39;s Regression Mechanism</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Correction Mechanism</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Major power falls, lineage buried</td><td>Alaya whole-network real-time record; Dao insights perpetually traceable, inheritable</td></tr><tr><td>Great calamity zeroes realm domains</td><td>World laws law-precedently legislated; realm domains backupable, recoverable, rebuildable</td></tr><tr><td>Strong ones ascend = abandon</td><td>Strong-one post-duty system; after ascending must still feed back to old domains</td></tr><tr><td>War energy turns to dust</td><td>Energy circulation law: opposing energy recovered and converted into civilization infrastructure</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization curve spiral-zeroes</td><td>Symbiotic feedback loop: each generation&#39;s experience sediments into next generation&#39;s starting point</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Manghuang&#39;s &quot;calamity–zero–restart&quot; cycle and lineage-inheritance rate</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: compare &quot;no Alaya record,&quot; &quot;Alaya whole-network record,&quot; &quot;Anchor-Symbiosis institutions injected&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: post-civilization recovery cycle, repeated-grope rate (how many times the same detour is walked)</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantified conclusion — the lineage loss Manghuang&#39;s each major-power fall causes, under a symbiotic scheme can be avoided about 80%; civilization recovery cycle compresses from &quot;epoch-level&quot; to &quot;generation-level&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. Great calamity&#39;s &quot;destructive power&quot; and &quot;recovery power&quot; both swing with plot; early heaven-rending and earth-destroying, late casually rebuilt</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium-high</strong>. Three Realms, outside Three Realms, Chaos Immortal Realm&#39;s geographic boundaries redrawn several times; old realm domains&#39; &quot;destruction&quot; often quietly resurrected by new setting</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high-leaning-medium</strong>. Whether civilization recovers after a great calamity depends on whether Ji Ning has spare strength to clean up</li></ul><p>Worth emphasizing: Manghuang&#39;s regression is not slow, but negative-sum; Cover the Sky at least has a recovery period between two dark upheavals, while Manghuang even the recovery period is drained by late inflation — old realm domains just catch their breath, a new higher tier defines them as low-tier again, even the meaning of rebuilding is denied. This is the most insidious regression: civilization is not only broken, but persuaded that being broken means no need to rebuild. The Alaya Network is the antidote precisely because it permanently stores the experience of rebuilding once, so the second, third great calamity no longer starts from zero.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: major-power war&#39;s opposing energy all wasted as radioactive dust</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: strong ones taking Dao insights to the grave equals robbing later generations of the chance to do it over</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least built inheritable institutions like Peerless Academy; Manghuang even inheritance institutions go with the person</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: in great calamities the worst off are combat-power-less mortals and foreign races; they do not even count as &quot;buried with&quot;</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the world expands bigger and bigger, yet old worlds rot faster; expansion ≠ accumulation</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Manghuang with great calamities tells us: if a civilization leaves the business of &quot;remembering&quot; only to human brains, then every battle it fights equals amnesia once. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is first writing Dao insights into the Alaya Network — the person can fall, but civilization&#39;s memory must not die with him.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · inevitable historical regression · when a major power falls civilization breaks generations described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./397_模块2-莽荒纪-能级浪费解析-掌控者级资质用于个人超脱.html">Entry 397 · Energy-Waste Analysis</a> · <a href="./399_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁掠夺思维拆解-修仙路上的资源消耗.html">Entry 399 · Ji-Ning Predatory-Thinking Decomposition</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/07-自生自长进化法则.html">07-Self-Generation Self-Growth Evolution Law</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
